--- 4. T511 reading ---
The stored T511 witness lift used a maximum TT15 chain C in T127 and found trans(D(D(C))) = 30. Twelve one-extra packets and eight two-extra packets with trans(X)=15 also stayed at 30.
Therefore the predicted T511=31 cannot be proved by a naked maximum chain. One must find a marked T127 support packet X with trans(X)=15 and trans(D(D(X)))>=31, or prove no such packet exists and look for a nonlocal witness.

